SUMMARY:John Mulaney: Mister Whatever LIVE at The Louisville Palace
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nJohn Mulaney is one of the most acclaimed and beloved stand-up comedians of his generation. A former Saturday Night Live writer\, Mulaney has released a string of critically celebrated Netflix specials including New in Town\, The Comeback Kid\, Kid Gorgeous\, and Baby J — each one earning him widespread praise for his impeccable storytelling\, sharp wit\, and masterful comedic timing. \nKnown for his clean-cut delivery and deeply personal material\, Mulaney has a rare ability to craft jokes that are simultaneously hilarious and deeply human. His comedy draws from his own life experiences — from his Catholic upbringing to his well-documented personal struggles — with a vulnerability and humor that resonates with audiences everywhere. \nMister Whatever is John Mulaney’s latest stand-up tour\, featuring all-new material that continues his evolution as one of comedy’s most gifted storytellers. This is a must-see show for comedy fans of all ages. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Thursday\, August 6\, 2026\nTime: 6:30 PM (Doors open)\nVenue: The Louisville Palace\, 625 S. 4th Street\, Louisville\, KY 40202\nAge Restrictions: All ages welcome\nTicket Price Range: $78 – $360\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Louisville Palace is one of the most breathtaking theaters in the American South. This Spanish Baroque masterpiece\, built in 1928\, seats approximately 2\,800 guests and is renowned for its ornate architecture\, gilded ceilings\, and grand interior that creates an unforgettable atmosphere for every performance. \nLocated at 625 S. 4th Street in the heart of downtown Louisville\, the venue is surrounded by the city’s best restaurants\, bars\, and hotels. The theater’s exceptional acoustics and sightlines ensure a premium experience from every seat in the house. \nParking is available in nearby downtown garages and surface lots. The venue is easily accessible via rideshare services and public transportation throughout Louisville. \nWhat to Expect\nJohn Mulaney: Mister Whatever is a full headline stand-up performance featuring all-new material. This is a solo show — just John\, a microphone\, and his extraordinary gift for storytelling and comedy. \nAudiences can expect Mulaney’s signature blend of perfectly crafted jokes\, hilarious personal anecdotes\, and the kind of masterful comedic timing that has made him one of the most in-demand performers in the world. His shows are consistently praised as some of the best live comedy experiences available. \nDoors open at 6:30 PM. Arrive early to find your seats and enjoy the stunning interior of The Louisville Palace before the show begins. \nTicket Information\nTickets range from $78 to $360 depending on seat location and package. Purchase official tickets through Ticketmaster or find resale tickets through VividSeats. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/john-mulaney-mister-whatever-live-at-the-louisville-palace/
LOCATION:The Louisville Palace\, 625 S. 4th Street\, Louisville\, Kentucky\, 40202\, United States Of America
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://media.ticketmaster.com/en-us/dam/a/b30/ccd9ebe2-c301-4487-bbe4-5bd6be744b30_TABLET_LANDSCAPE_LARGE_16_9.jpg
GEO:38.2480515;-85.7578327
