SUMMARY:Rene Vaca LIVE at Raleigh Improv
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nRene Vaca is a rising star in the world of stand-up comedy\, born and raised in the San Fernando Valley of Southern California. His journey to the stage is as compelling as his comedy — after his father was incarcerated\, Vaca started his own landscaping business at just 15 years old to support himself. He later earned acceptance to the University of California\, Merced\, where he began pursuing his true passion: making people laugh. \nVaca’s hard work paid off in a big way when he won the prestigious 16th Annual StandUp NBC competition\, one of the most respected comedy competitions in the country. Since then\, he has shared the stage with comedy legends including Bill Burr\, Ken Jeong\, Amir K.\, and Jamie Kennedy. His 2025 Netflix special Live in Portland introduced him to millions of new fans\, and his social media presence — with over 2 million followers — continues to grow rapidly. \nKnown for his fearless crowd work\, sharp personal storytelling\, and clean callbacks that land with explosive energy\, Rene Vaca delivers a show that feels both intimate and electric. His comedy draws from real life — his upbringing\, his hustle\, and his unique perspective as a first-generation college graduate who made it on his own terms. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Friday\, August 7\, 2026\nShow Time: 7:00 PM EDT\nDoors Open: 5:30 PM EDT\nVenue: Raleigh Improv\nAddress: 1224 Parkside Main St\, Cary\, NC 27519\nAge Restriction: 21+ (Valid ID required)\nSeating: General Admission\, first-come first-served (except groups and premium booths)\nNote: Two-item minimum purchase per person in the showroom. No cell phones\, photography\, or video recording during the performance.\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Raleigh Improv is the Triangle area’s premier comedy club\, located at 1224 Parkside Main St in Cary\, NC — just minutes from downtown Raleigh. Part of the nationally recognized Improv Comedy Club chain\, the Raleigh Improv has hosted some of the biggest names in stand-up comedy and continues to be the go-to destination for world-class comedy in the Research Triangle. \nThe venue features a classic comedy club layout with a main showroom that offers excellent sightlines from every seat. The intimate atmosphere ensures that no matter where you sit\, you’ll feel close to the action. The club offers a full food and beverage menu\, with a mandatory two-item minimum per guest — making it a perfect dinner-and-a-show experience. Premium booth seating is available for groups looking for a more elevated experience\, complete with food and beverage credits. \nThe Raleigh Improv is conveniently located in the Parkside Town Commons shopping center in Cary\, with ample free parking available in the surrounding lot. The venue is easily accessible from I-40 and US-1\, making it a convenient destination for comedy fans from Raleigh\, Durham\, Chapel Hill\, and the surrounding Research Triangle area. \nWhat to Expect\nRene Vaca’s live show is a high-energy\, crowd-interactive experience that blends personal storytelling with sharp observational humor. Expect Vaca to work the room with his signature fearless crowd work — he’s known for turning audience interactions into some of the funniest moments of the night. His set weaves together stories from his upbringing in the San Fernando Valley\, his entrepreneurial hustle\, and his rapid rise in the comedy world. \nThis is a solo headlining show\, so you’ll get a full set from Rene Vaca himself. The show runs approximately 90 minutes to two hours. Given the 21+ age restriction\, this is an adults-only evening of comedy — arrive early to grab a drink\, find your seat\, and settle in before the laughs begin. Doors open at 5:30 PM\, giving you plenty of time to enjoy the full club experience before the 7:00 PM showtime. \nFans of comedians like Bill Burr\, Bert Kreischer\, and Felipe Esparza will feel right at home with Rene Vaca’s style — raw\, honest\, and genuinely funny. This is one of the hottest up-and-coming comedians in the country\, and catching him at an intimate venue like the Raleigh Improv is a rare opportunity. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $25 – $75 (plus fees) \n\nGA Ticket: $25 (+ fees)\nGA Booth for 4: $75/person (includes $200 food & beverage credit)\nVIP Meet & Greet Ticket: $70 (+ fees)\nPremium Booth for 4: $90/person (includes $200 food & beverage credit)\n\nTickets are available through the official Ticketmaster/TicketWeb link below. Note: The Raleigh Improv strictly prohibits ticket resale — purchase only through official channels. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/rene-vaca-live-at-raleigh-improv/
LOCATION:Raleigh Improv\, 1224 Parkside Main St\, Cary\, NC\, 27519\, United States Of America
