SUMMARY:Tiffany Haddish LIVE at Chicago Improv
DESCRIPTION:This post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nTiffany Haddish is one of the most celebrated comedic talents of her generation. An Emmy Award winner\, Grammy Award winner\, and NAACP Image Award recipient\, Haddish has established herself as one of the most sought-after performers in Hollywood and on the stand-up stage. \nBest known for her breakout performance in the smash hit Girls Trip\, Haddish has since starred in Bad Boys: Ride or Die\, Apple TV+’s The Afterparty\, and The Unbearable Weight of Massive Talent. She won the Emmy Award for hosting Saturday Night Live — becoming the first Black female stand-up comedian to host the show — and a Grammy for her comedy special Tiffany Haddish: Black Mitzvah. She is also a New York Times bestselling author of The Last Black Unicorn. \nCurrently on her Funny and Fearless Tour\, Haddish is bringing a brand-new stand-up set to audiences across the country. Expect raw\, honest\, and deeply funny storytelling from one of comedy’s brightest stars. Her comedy draws from her remarkable life story — growing up in foster care\, overcoming adversity\, and finding her voice through laughter. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Friday\, August 7\, 2026\nShow Time: 7:00 PM CDT (Doors open at 5:00 PM)\nSecond Show: 9:30 PM CDT also available\nAdditional Shows: Saturday August 8 (7:00 PM & 9:30 PM) and Sunday August 9 (6:00 PM)\nVenue: Chicago Improv\nAddress: 5 Woodfield Mall K120B\, Schaumburg\, IL 60173\nAge Restriction: 21+ only. Valid ID required at entry.\nTicket Prices: $38 GA / $52 VIP (plus fees)\nNote: Two-item minimum purchase per person in the showroom. No photography or video recording during the show. All sales are final.\n\nAbout the Venue\nChicago Improv is the Chicago area’s premier comedy club\, located inside the Woodfield Mall in Schaumburg\, Illinois — just 30 miles northwest of downtown Chicago. Part of the nationally recognized Improv comedy club chain\, Chicago Improv has hosted some of the biggest names in stand-up comedy for decades. \nThe showroom features general admission seating with host-escorted placement\, ensuring every guest gets a great view of the stage. The intimate club atmosphere puts you right in the middle of the action\, with a full bar and a mandatory two-item minimum per guest. VIP and premium booth seating is available for groups\, offering a more exclusive experience with premium viewing. \nThe venue is easily accessible from I-90 and Route 53\, with ample parking available throughout the Woodfield Mall complex. The surrounding mall offers plenty of dining and shopping options for a complete night out in the suburbs. Chicago Improv is a 21+ venue for all shows. \nWhat to Expect\nThis is a solo headlining stand-up performance by Tiffany Haddish as part of her Funny and Fearless Tour. Expect a high-energy\, deeply personal\, and laugh-out-loud funny show from one of the biggest names in comedy today. Haddish is known for her infectious energy\, crowd interaction\, and willingness to share the most personal and outrageous stories from her life. \nHer shows feel like a conversation with your funniest\, most real friend — warm\, wild\, and completely unforgettable. This is a rare chance to see an Emmy and Grammy-winning comedian in an intimate club setting. Multiple shows are available across the weekend (August 7-9)\, so there are plenty of opportunities to catch this incredible performer. Arrive early to grab a drink and a great seat before the show begins. \nTicket Information\nPrice: $38 GA ($50.05 with fees) / $52 VIP ($68.30 with fees) \nTickets are available through Ticketmaster (official) and VividSeats (resale). This is a 21+ event. All sales are final — no refunds or exchanges. Tiffany Haddish shows sell out fast — secure your seats now! \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/tiffany-haddish-live-at-chicago-improv/
